# GitHub Actions Secrets Configuration
# Setup these secrets in: Repository Settings > Secrets and variables > Actions

## AWS Credentials
AWS_ACCESS_KEY_ID=your-aws-access-key-id
AWS_SECRET_ACCESS_KEY=your-aws-secret-key
AWS_REGION=ap-southeast-1

## SSH Keys
SSH_PRIVATE_KEY_STAGING=your-staging-ssh-private-key
SSH_PRIVATE_KEY_PROD=your-production-ssh-private-key

## EC2 Hosts
EC2_HOST_STAGING=staging.finlapor.com (or IP)
EC2_HOST_PROD=api.finlapor.com (or IP)

## API URLs
STAGING_API_URL=https://staging-api.finlapor.com
PROD_API_URL=https://api.finlapor.com

## Database
DATABASE_URL_PROD=postgres://user:pass@host:5432/finlapor?sslmode=require

## CloudFlare
CLOUDFLARE_API_TOKEN=your-cloudflare-token
CLOUDFLARE_ACCOUNT_ID=your-account-id

## Notifications
SLACK_WEBHOOK_URL=https://hooks.slack.com/services/your/webhook/url

## Notes:
# - Never commit actual secrets to Git
# - Use GitHub Secrets for all sensitive values
# - Rotate secrets regularly
# - Use different secrets for staging and production
